\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline Part 1: is the silver/bronze standard better than GOI's own output?}{58}{paragraph*.190}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline Part 2: once the silver standard existed, did tuning and fine-tuning the pipeline against it actually help?}{60}{paragraph*.192}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline Limitation: precision is a lower bound, not an exact figure.}{61}{paragraph*.194}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline A second, distinct bias: active-learning sampling skews which relevant companies get verified, not just how many.}{62}{paragraph*.196}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline A third bias, harder to quantify: the author personally breaks judge disagreements, then those decisions score the author's own system.}{62}{paragraph*.198}%
